html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>R10 vs R9 · compact core and native attributes</title><style>body{margin:16px;background:#101b25;color:#e5edf4;font:16px system-ui}a{color:#a6def5}button,select{font:inherit;padding:5px;margin:5px}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}figure{margin:0;min-width:0;background:#192b3a}figcaption{padding:8px}.frame{overflow:auto;max-height:76vh}img{display:block;width:100%}.native img{width:auto;max-width:none}.native .frame{height:560px}p{max-width:1100px}h1{font-size:1.4em}</style><h1>R10 candidate · compact core + 38 native attributes</h1><p>The routine You summary keeps the twelve native combat stats in a smaller grid. Attributes opens the existing Stats home, uses the full center pane, and adds group filters, a With modifiers filter, base/current values and native modifier categories. Reports stays visible. Back/Esc restores the previous view.</p><p><a href="/r10-demo.html" target="_blank">Play R10 · synthetic save</a> · <a href="../../R10_REPORT.md">Audit, checks and limits</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:19167/docs/gm/dispatch/ui-foundation-2026-10-15/evidence/parity-r9/comparison.html">R9 multi-enemy comparison</a></p><p>Actual native recovery, efficiency, environment and XP fields only. Dormant fields are identified in detail. Aggregate source categories do not imply individual gem/item attribution. Comprehensive lists use bounded local scrolling instead of reducing the chosen font size.</p><label>Screen/text <select id="size"></select></label><label>View <select id="mode"><option value="core">Routine You</option><option value="attributes">Stats reference</option></select></label><button id="scale">Toggle native pixels / fit images</button><div class="pair"><figure><figcaption>R9 · preserved <a id="left-link" target="_blank">Full image</a></figcaption><div class="frame"><img id="left" alt="R9 at matching screen and font size"></div></figure><figure><figcaption>R10 · rebuilt <a id="right-link" target="_blank">Full image</a></figcaption><div class="frame"><img id="right" alt="R10 at matching screen and font size"></div></figure></div><p>Six desktop/font cases: 1366×768 at 14/17.5/21px, 1920×1080, 2560×1440 and 3600×1906 at21px. Technical browser checks are separate from your visual/play acceptance, which remains open. No personal saves used.</p><script>const cases=CASES,size=document.getElementById('size'),mode=document.getElementById('mode');cases.forEach(([w,f],i)=>size.add(new Option(w+'px · '+f+'px text',i)));size.value=2;function update(){const[w,f]=cases[size.value];for(const side of ['left','right']){const path=(side==='left'?'r9-':'')+mode.value+'-'+w+'-'+f+'.png';document.getElementById(side).src=path;document.getElementById(side+'-link').href=path;}}size.onchange=mode.onchange=update;document.getElementById('scale').onclick=()=>document.body.classList.toggle('native');update();</script></html>'''.replace('CASES',json.dumps(cases))
(e/'comparison.html').write_text(html)
